$\quad \mathrm{fog}(\mathrm{x})=\mathrm{f}(\mathrm{g}(\mathrm{x}))$
$$\begin{array}{l}
=f\left(\frac{2-3 x}{1-x}\right)=\frac{2\left(\frac{2-3 x}{1-x}\right)+3}{5\left(\frac{2-3 x}{1-x}\right)+2} \\
=\frac{4-6 x+3-3 x}{10-15 x+2-2 x}=\left(\frac{7-9 x}{12-17 x}\right) \\
\therefore\left[\begin{array}{c}
12-7 x \neq 0 \\
x \neq \frac{12}{17}
\end{array}\right. \\
{\left[\begin{array}{c}
\text { fog }(2)=\frac{7-9(2)}{12-17(2)}=\frac{-11}{-22}=\frac{1}{2} \\
\text { fog }(4)=\frac{7-9(4)}{12-17(4)}=\frac{-29}{-56}=\frac{29}{56} \\
\text { Range of fog : }[\alpha, \beta]=\left[\frac{1}{2}, \frac{29}{56}\right] \\
\therefore(\beta-\alpha)=\frac{29}{56}-\frac{1}{2}=\frac{29-28}{56}=\frac{1}{56} \\
\frac{1}{(\beta-\alpha)}=56
\end{array}\right.}
\end{array}$$

Now using work energy theorem
$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{W}_{\mathrm{g}}=\Delta \mathrm{k} \\
-\mathrm{mg} \ell(1-\cos \theta)=0-\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{mv}^{2} \\
\mathrm{~g} \ell\left(2 \sin ^{2} \frac{\theta}{2}\right)=\frac{\mathrm{v}^{2}}{2}
\end{array}$$
as $\theta$ is small
$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{g} \ell 2\left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{2} \frac{4 \mathrm{E}^{2}}{\mathrm{~m}^{2} \mathrm{c}^{2}} \quad \text { (from eq. (1)) } \\
\mathrm{g} \ell \theta^{2}=\frac{4 \mathrm{E}^{2}}{\mathrm{~m}^{2} \mathrm{c}^{2}} \\
\theta=\frac{2 \mathrm{E}}{\mathrm{mc} \sqrt{\mathrm{~g} \ell}}
\end{array}$$

