$\mathrm{r}_{1}=\mathrm{k}[\mathrm{A}]^{\mathrm{n}}[\mathrm{B}]^{\mathrm{m}}$
Now A is doubled \& B is halved in concentration
$$\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow \mathrm{r}_{2}=\mathrm{k} 2^{\mathrm{n}}[\mathrm{~A}]^{\mathrm{n}} \cdot \frac{[\mathrm{~B}]^{\mathrm{m}}}{2^{\mathrm{m}}} \\
\text { Now } \frac{\mathrm{r}_{2}}{\mathrm{r}_{1}}=2^{(\mathrm{n}-\mathrm{m})}
\end{array}$$
